nicholss@magellan.Colorado.EDU (NICHOLS  SCOTT CONRAD) writes:

>I just started playing NetHack (3.1 Amiga), I keep starving to death.  How
>do I find food?  I've tried to eat the corpses of my victims, but its
>usually bad for me, what do I do?  What is the best character?  Is this

Probably the trouble is that you eat too OLD corpses. Don't eat any corpses
you haven't killed (or seen die) within, let's say, 15 moves. (Actually
the time is different for different kinds of monsters, and you may learn
which ones stay edible longer, but you could start with that rule of thumb.)
If the meat tastes tainted, it was too old. If it just tastes terrible,
it was fresh enough. If it burns like acid, it is usually better to avoid that
kind of corpses (except for when your limbs are stiffening.)
You could find some spoiler file to learn more specific hints, but you'll
probably find out most of what is edible and what isn't after some time of
playing.

The best character.. that depends somewhat on your style of playing.
Samurais and valkyries are good fighters and start with good weapon/armor.
They are the easiest ones to get high scores with.
Barbarians and elves are also good fighters.
Priests always know which items are cursed and which are blessed, but they
are hard to keep alive very deep in the dungeon.
The rest are more challenging, especially for inexperienced players.
